; a universally quantified part of a conjunctive premise, like the induction step in
; natural.kurt's "induction", is looked up among the stored facts without its outer `forall`
; (stored facts have theirs removed) -- but its fresh variable must stay generic: one
; specific instance `Q c` must not count as `forall $x (Q $x)`.
load prop
bool Q, R, S
arity Q 1
const c
use ((forall $x (Q $x)) and R) implies S   "ax"
use R
use Q c
expect "ProofError"
    S

; a genuinely universal fact does satisfy the premise
use forall $y (Q $y)
S
